<p><strong>Amazon S3 Versioning</strong></p>

<p>Versioning is a means of keeping multiple variants of an object in the s=
ame bucket. You can use versioning to preserve, retrieve, and restore every=
 version of every object stored in your Amazon S3 bucket. With versioning, =
you can easily recover from both unintended user actions and application fa=
ilures.</p>

<p>Versioning-enabled buckets enable you to recover objects from accidental=
 deletion or overwrite. For example: if you delete an object, instead of re=
moving it permanently, Amazon S3 inserts a delete marker, which becomes the=
 current object version.</p>

<p>Amazon S3 Versioning Overview:
